        "predicate": "summary",
        "object": "<p>After Lindsey Graham’s death, Democrat Annie Andrews finds herself in a closely watched race as she seeks to flip his Republican seat</p><p>Annie Andrews was a dark horse Democrat challenging a five-term Republican in the US Senate when 314 Action, a political action fund devoted to electing scientists and doctors, first backed her.</p><p>Now, after the unexpected death of Senator Lindsey Graham, Andrews finds herself in a closely watched race. Donald Trump persuaded South Carolina voters last week to <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/aug/25/south-carolina-senate-republican-primary-runoff\">select Graham’s sister, Darline</a>, as the new Republican candidate. They will face off in November in an election still heavily favored to keep the seat in Republican hands in the conservative state.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/aug/31/annie-andrews-south-carolina-senate\">Continue reading...</a>"
